body:
### Description

GPT5 with `web_search_preview` tool consistently throws with `APICallError [AI_APICallError]: Invalid JSON response`.  Although in logging middleware I can see that the search was performed and generally the output looked fine. Looks to me that some internal vercel/ai sdk validation for `web_search_preview` has a bug. I believe this zod schema is too strict, as in my tests sometimes `action` has only `type` field (see example in comments below)

https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/5f85d6f6cb4fa310d6014df82d5572695e6e734f/packages/openai/src/tool/web-search-preview.ts#L90




```
export const chatGpt5 = wrapLanguageModel({
  model: openai('gpt-5'),
  middleware: [llmLoggingMiddleware],
})

const chatGpt5ModelAndSettings = {
  model: chatGpt5,
  temperature: 0.1,
}

const generateResult = await generateText({
    ...chatGpt5ModelAndSettings,
    tools: {
      //https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/tools-web-search?api-mode=responses
      web_search_preview: openai.tools.webSearchPreview({
        searchContextSize: 'high',
      }),
    },
    // Force web search tool:
    // Currently doesn't work due to a bug: https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/8201
    // toolChoice: { type: 'tool', toolName: 'web_search_preview' },
    abortSignal,
    messages: [...]
  })
```

```
error: APICallError [AI_APICallError]: Invalid JSON response
   at file:///Users/xx/Sites/xx/node_modules/.pnpm/@ai-sdk+provider-utils@3.0.5_zod@4.0.14/node_modules/@ai-sdk/provider-utils/src/response-handler.ts:151:13
  at processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)
  at postToApi (file:///Users/xx/Sites/xx/node_modules/.pnpm/@ai-sdk+provider-utils@3.0.5_zod@4.0.14/node_modules/@ai-sdk/provider-utils/src/post-to-api.ts:136:14)
```

